{
  "sequence": [
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "text": "HOW IT WORKS"
    },
    {
      "type": "H1",
      "id": "title",
      "text": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "text": "A language model that looks things up in your documents before it answers."
    },
    {
      "type": "Figure",
      "id": "arrows",
      "alt": "Flow diagram in two lanes that share a vector store. Lane A, done ahead of time: documents are split into chunks, each chunk is embedded, and the embed step writes vector + text + source ID into the vector store. Lane B, every time someone asks: the question is embedded with the same model; the query vector is sent to the vector store, which returns the top-k chunks + source IDs to the retrieve step; then augment, generate and answer follow in order, and a dashed line shows that the original question travels with the retrieved context."
    },
    {
      "type": "H2",
      "id": "lane_ingest",
      "text": "A  /  INDEX YOUR KNOWLEDGE  /  DONE AHEAD OF TIME"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "docs_step",
      "text": "01"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "docs_title",
      "text": "Documents"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "docs_desc",
      "text": "PDFs, wikis, tickets and notes"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "chunk_step",
      "text": "02"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "chunk_title",
      "text": "Chunk"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "chunk_desc",
      "text": "Split into passages; keep each source ID"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "embed_index_step",
      "text": "03"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "embed_index_title",
      "text": "Embed"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "embed_index_desc",
      "text": "A model turns each chunk into a vector"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "edge_write",
      "text": "vector + text + source ID"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "store_step",
      "text": "04"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "store_title",
      "text": "Vector store"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "store_desc",
      "text": "Vectors, chunk text and source IDs"
    },
    {
      "type": "H2",
      "id": "panel_stored_title",
      "text": "WHAT GETS STORED"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "panel_stored_body",
      "text": "Each chunk is saved three ways: its text, its embedding vector, and the ID of the source it came from."
    },
    {
      "type": "H2",
      "id": "lane_query",
      "text": "B  /  ANSWER A QUESTION  /  EVERY TIME SOMEONE ASKS"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "question_step",
      "text": "05"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "question_title",
      "text": "Question"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "question_desc",
      "text": "\"What is our refund window?\""
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "embed_query_step",
      "text": "06"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "embed_query_title",
      "text": "Embed"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "embed_query_desc",
      "text": "Same model, same vector space"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "edge_query_vector",
      "text": "query vector"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "edge_chunks",
      "text": "top-k chunks + source IDs"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "retrieve_step",
      "text": "07"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "retrieve_title",
      "text": "Retrieve"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "retrieve_desc",
      "text": "Nearest chunks to the question"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "augment_step",
      "text": "08"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "augment_title",
      "text": "Augment"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "augment_desc",
      "text": "Question plus retrieved chunks and IDs"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "edge_question",
      "text": "the original question travels with the retrieved context"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "llm_step",
      "text": "09"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "llm_title",
      "text": "Generate"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "llm_desc",
      "text": "Answers using only the given context"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "answer_step",
      "text": "10"
    },
    {
      "type": "H3",
      "id": "answer_title",
      "text": "Answer"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "answer_desc",
      "text": "Cites its sources: [1] [2]"
    },
    {
      "type": "H2",
      "id": "panel_why_title",
      "text": "WHY RETRIEVE FIRST"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "panel_why_body",
      "text": "The model answers from your documents, not only from its training, and can point to where each fact came from."
    },
    {
      "type": "H2",
      "id": "panel_how_title",
      "text": "HOW RETRIEVAL WORKS"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "panel_how_body",
      "text": "The question becomes a vector. The store returns the k chunks whose vectors sit nearest to it; k is a setting you choose."
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "footer_message",
      "text": "INDEX ONCE  /  RETRIEVE  /  AUGMENT  /  GENERATE"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "footer_credit",
      "text": "XYZ LAYOUT ENGINE"
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "scale_note",
      "text": "Conceptual diagram: real systems differ in chunk size, embedding model, store and ranking. Icons are hand-drawn vector art; no images were generated."
    },
    {
      "type": "P",
      "id": "source_note",
      "text": "Pattern: Lewis et al., \"Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP Tasks\" (2020), arXiv:2005.11401"
    }
  ],
